# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.example IS committed; .env never is.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/testdata/**/*.key      # deliberately-fake keys used by signing tests
secrets/

# --- OSINT tool artifacts --------------------------------------------------
# Scanner binaries and vulnerability databases are FETCHED AND VERIFIED, never
# committed. OSINT/tools.manifest.yaml is the only committed OSINT artifact —
# it pins versions, digests and checksums. See docs/04-OSINT-INTEGRATION.md.
.axebom/
OSINT/bin/
OSINT/src/
OSINT/.venv/
OSINT/cache/

# --- Scan workspaces -------------------------------------------------------
# Cloned user repositories. Untrusted content — must never reach the repo.
workspaces/
tmp/

# --- Go --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
/bin/
/dist/
vendor/

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Node / frontend -------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Editors / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Local infrastructure state -------------------------------------------
deploy/compose/.data/
*.local.yml

# --- Third-party reference checkouts ---------------------------------------
# `.reference/zitadel` is a pinned, READ-ONLY checkout of the ZITADEL server,
# used to read its `cmd/defaults.yaml`, its compose reference stack and its
# Apache-2.0 `proto/` while building our provisioner.
#
# ⚠ IT IS NEVER VENDORED, IMPORTED OR BUILT. The ZITADEL server is AGPL-3.0
# (everything outside `proto/`, `apps/docs/`, `apps/login/` and `packages/`),
# and CLAUDE.md invariant 9 puts copyleft in a separate service, never in our
# binaries. We run the published container; we link only the Apache-2.0
# `zitadel-go` / `zitadel/oidc` modules. `.golangci.yml` has a depguard rule
# that fails the build on any `github.com/zitadel/zitadel/...` import, so this
# cannot regress by accident.
.reference/

# --- Test / coverage output ------------------------------------------------
coverage.out
coverage.html
# Unanchored: Playwright runs from frontend/, so these appear at
# frontend/test-results/ and a leading slash would only ignore the root copy.
playwright-report/
test-results/

# --- Generated code IS committed -------------------------------------------
# The model files under libs/go-shared/model/ and
# libs/py-shared/axebom_shared/model/ are produced by `task profile:gen`
# but deliberately NOT ignored:
#
#   - a fresh clone must `go build` without first running a codegen step
#   - the diff is the review surface when the compliance profile changes,
#     which is exactly the change that most deserves a human reading it
#
# Drift is caught by the `profile-drift` CI job, which regenerates and fails on
# any difference — the same pattern as the service generator.

# --- Genuinely generated, not committed ------------------------------------
proto/gen/
# The `axebom` CLI binary, if someone runs `go build ./cmd/...` from the repo
# root. The CLI is invoked with `go run ./cmd/axebom`, so a committed binary is
# always stale and platform-specific.
axebom
